\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Definition}
\title{The exterior rotational action}
\date{2026-11-17}

\p{For the \vocabk{internal exterior module}{fdip-00YE}, let #{\Gamma} and #{\rho}
be the Clifford group and its vector action from
\ref{fdip-00OB}. Choose any subgroup #{H\subseteq\Gamma} such
that every #{\rho(R)}, #{R\in H}, preserves #{b}; #{H} need not
be finite. The \vocab{exterior rotational action} is
#{A(R)=\Lambda(\rho(R))} on #{E}, defined by #{A(R)1=1} and
##{A(R)(v_1\wedge\cdots\wedge v_p)
 =\rho(R)v_1\wedge\cdots\wedge\rho(R)v_p.}}
